notes.content:
Import scheme: flat. Run: python main.py. Smoke: echo quit | python main.py. Files: models.py, data_loader.py, parser.py, combat.py, game_state.py, world.yaml, main.py.
Data shapes:
  world.yaml → data_loader.py: Mapping with top-level keys: rooms, items, npcs, monsters, boss, start_room_id. Rooms reference items/NPCs/monsters by id.
State contracts:
  GameState (owner models.py, consumers engine.py, game_state.py, combat.py): {player: Player, current_room_id: str, inventory: list of item_ids, equipped: {slot: item_id}, room_states: {room_id: {items: [item_id], npcs: [npc_id], monster: monster_id | null}}, npc_dialogue_progress: {npc_id: int}, defeated_monsters: set of monster_ids, boss_defeated: bool}
  Player (owner models.py, consumers engine.py, combat.py, game_state.py): {health: int, max_health: int, attack: int, defense: int, inventory: list of item_ids, equipped: {slot: item_id}}
  load_world() return / GameEngine.__init__ input (owner data_loader.py, consumers engine.py, main.py): {rooms: {room_id: Room}, items: {item_id: Item}, npcs: {npc_id: NPC}, monsters: {monster_id: Monster}, boss: Boss, start_room_id: str} — exactly these top-level keys
  save file JSON (owner game_state.py, consumers game_state.py): {player: {health: int, max_health: int, attack: int, defense: int, inventory: [item_id], equipped: {slot: item_id}}, current_room_id: str, room_states: {room_id: {items: [item_id], npcs: [npc_id], monster: monster_id | null}}, npc_dialogue_progress: {npc_id: int}, defeated_monsters: [monster_id], boss_defeated: bool}
  Command (owner parser.py, consumers engine.py): {type: CommandType, direction: Direction | null, item_id: str | null, npc_id: str | null, monster_id: str | null}
